# Trivy misconfiguration findings accepted for deploy/k8s (the `containers` job, trivy config).
# Each entry was reviewed; add a new one only with the reason on the line above it.

# KSV-0109 (HIGH) postgres.yaml, ConfigMap postgres-init: false positive. The init script reads the
# role passwords from environment variables injected from a Secret; the ConfigMap holds no secret.
KSV-0109

# KSV-0014 (HIGH) postgres.yaml: the upstream PostgreSQL image's entrypoint writes to several system
# paths, so the root filesystem stays writable. Documented in the manifest; the container is
# otherwise restricted (non-root, seccomp RuntimeDefault).
KSV-0014

# KSV-0041 (CRITICAL) rbac-mcp.yaml, ClusterRole pydanticos-mcp-tenant: by design. The role is only
# ever bound by RoleBindings inside one mcp-tenant-* namespace, so it grants Secret access in that
# tenant's namespace only, by name (no list or watch). The MCP runtime needs it to store each
# managed server's credentials.
KSV-0041

# KSV-0056 (HIGH) rbac-mcp.yaml, same role: by design. The role manages the NetworkPolicies of that
# one tenant namespace (the per-tenant policies the adapter creates), again only via per-namespace
# RoleBindings.
KSV-0056
